implementationPlan.description:
RE-VERIFY THE TWO DEFECTS AND THE DESIGN THAT RESOLVES THEM. worker-7bdbffac parked the previous plan on these; do not write until you have reproduced both.

DEFECT 2 (the serious one): `readCurrentProductContractRevisionV2` answers CURRENT, not APPROVED. Confirm a current revision can be unapproved - the worker cites store.test:136 reading a new revision before approval. Publishing proposal names into a COMMITTED `.env.example` would breach DoD 1 and put names nobody approved into a product repository.
THE PRECEDENT TO COPY is apps/daemon/src/delivery-v2/resolution-selection-reader.ts:177-183:
  const current = readCurrentProductContractRevisionV2(store, { contractId, projectId });
  if (!current.ok) return current;
  const ref = Object.freeze({ contractId: current.revision.contractId,
    revisionDigest: current.revision.revisionDigest, revisionId: current.revision.revisionId });
  const gate = resolveProductContractGate1V2(store, { projectId, ref });
  if (!gate.ok) return gate;
Read those lines before writing step 2.

DEFECT 1: `grep -n "repository.bootstrap" apps/daemon/src/daemon-command-vocabulary.test.ts` - expect a roster row near :235 pinning `payloadKeys: ["dir","github","productName","profileVersion"]`, a SECOND transcriber beside the registry test. It is real. IT ONLY MOVES IF A COMMAND PAYLOAD KEY CHANGES, and under this plan none does: the names are read server-side, never supplied in the payload. CONFIRM your step-3 change adds a field to `BootstrapRequest` (repository-bootstrap-contracts.ts:61-67) and NOT to PAYLOAD_KEYS.
IF YOU FIND YOURSELF NEEDING A PAYLOAD KEY, STOP - that is a different design, it drags in two rosters four other rows are contending, and it would let an operator supply names the contract never required.

Re-verify the producer and generator are unchanged: environment-required-variables.ts:90, controlled-profile-generator.ts:63 and :138, controlled-profile-root-templates.ts:170.
